{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947963-modes-of-play","id":947963,"title":"Modes of Play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-10T12:44:11-07:00","id":947963,"title":"Modes of Play","content":"So this is an idea that Demon recently toyed with in it's Storyteller Guide and a handful of other games on the market have started doing as well; modes of play, or modular rules that help reinforce certain genre and theme subdivisions within a given game. The Demon STG gives us two axis, Soft/Loud (a sliding scale of action from slow-paced, deliberate paranoia at Soft to explosive action and car chases at Loud) and Smooth/ Rough (a sort of measure of grittiness, from cinematic &quot;the good guys are daring enough to dramatically pull it off&quot; to a nail-biting every bullet counts grind). Other games similarly explore these, primarily in GUMSHOE engine games (Trail of Cthulhu has Purist mode for doomed Lovecraftian horror and Pulp mode for action-horror where the heroes stand a chance, Night's Black Agents explores both a variety of espionage stories and a variety of vampire types, etc), and it adds a lot to the options for play.<br /> <br /> CofD as a whole has an informal divide in the fanbase between thematic purists and people who like to steer things in their own direction, and I figure adopting modes to the wider CofD (beyond a handful of options tucked into a Demon supplement) can only be a good thing, especially with the toolbox design goal at the outset of the nWoD and the success of books like Mirrors or various Chronicler's Guides.<br /> <br /> In this thread, I want to toss around ideas for what modes and axis would fit best in other CofD games, especially some of the more contentious ones. Would Vampire benefit from something representing the line between a spiral of humanity and morality (the personal horror the game is currently focused on) and more of a dark action feel, or maybe going in the opposite direction and doubling down on the necessity of Touchstones and the struggles of nightly hunger and feeding? Perhaps Hunter could offer options for the loss of normalcy and personal relationships (not to mention the threat of The Code warping your morality and possibly turning you into a Slasher) under the strain of the Vigil, or two-fisted drama that's kin to Hellboy and Van Helsing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:01:40-07:00","id":947976,"title":"","content":"You could probably make that a division between Internal or External. Is the game more about the characters, their development and growth of personality and power? Or are the characters mostly 'done' and the game focused on NPCs and the growth of PCs is primarily in the addition of abilities?<br /> <br /> I'm curious with how the modes of play tell. Is it just for advertising for groups? 'I'm running a Soft and Rough game of Demon, who would like to join?' Or is it similar to the mood and theme of the game, something you decide at the beginning and try to stick to throughout play? Basically, other than increasingly defining what kind of game you're running, what impact does choosing a mode of play have on play itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:11:03-07:00","id":947987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/947963-modes-of-play?p=947976#post947976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could probably make that a division between Internal or External. Is the game more about the characters, their development and growth of personality and power? Or are the characters mostly 'done' and the game focused on NPCs and the growth of PCs is primarily in the addition of abilities?<br /> <br /> I'm curious with how the modes of play tell. Is it just for advertising for groups? 'I'm running a Soft and Rough game of Demon.' Or is it similar to the mood and theme of the game, something you decide at the beginning and try to stick to throughout play? Basically, other than increasingly defining what kind of game you're running, what impact does choosing a mode of play have on play itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some variant rules associated with each. In the Demon Storyteller's Guide, the various pairs of the Soft/Loud and Smooth/Rough have some minor variants on character creation, and the aforementioned GUMSHOE games add whole new mechanics (the modes in Night's Black Agents do things like add Trust ratings between the player characters or remove the more fantastic abilities from characters). If you go back into 1e, Vampire has a delightful supplement called Danse Macabre that had variant rules for tiers of play, like Tier 1 chronicles having more frequent but shorther-lived Frenzy and removing clans in favor of building your own.<br /> <br /> In a harsher Promethean chronicle, you may have Disquiet build over a course of scenes rather than sessions, or bring back 1e's idea that Wastelands force the Created to stay on the move forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T13:29:42-07:00","id":948003,"title":"","content":"Another example is how lethal combat is intended to be. Hurt Locker has expanded &quot;damage as Conditions&quot; rules that can tweak values. Options for making it less lethal include rolling stamina to downgrade damage, or adding in the option to take Tilts or Conditions in place of damage (like in FATE with Consequences). More lethal could be as easy as reducing Health, upping damage ratings, or having attacks always inflict Tilts or Conditions on hit.<br /> <br /> Social aspects can be tweaked as easily as using the Social Maneuvering system (to make it longer, usually) or just making it a few (extended or not) rolls.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T16:34:41-07:00","id":948168,"title":"","content":"I would also recommend <b><i>Armory 2</i></b>. Its a little out of date now,but it has a nice section on &quot;Rule Hacks&quot; for fine-tuning mood and genre. Definitely worth a look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T17:48:28-07:00","id":948203,"title":"","content":"Drama/Mundanity could be one axis. How much of the time in your game is spent on scenes that are slice of life and how much time is spent on more dramatic or &quot;important&quot; events and situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T20:53:27-07:00","id":949072,"title":"","content":"In addition to the &quot;pulp action vs. psychological horror&quot; axis, I've also found that an interesting tone scale to use is sort of the human vs. cosmic axis, to differentiate moods within the horror genre. Basically, on one end you have Breaking Bad with magic, where it's dark and horrifying but primarily driven by human impulses: greed, lust, envy, prejudice, apathy, and so on. The supernatural is a tool, not as scary because of its inherent character as because of what it gives people the power to do. On the cosmic end, however, the antagonistic forces tend to be unfathomable, and often beyond any sort of human morality at all, without easily understandable motivations, that act more like forces of nature than defined individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}